1084:| `change_request_candidate_drift` | the worktree moved after the revision was published; rework and republish |
1085:| `change_request_revision_conflict` | expected-revision CAS failed; re-read the current revision |
1086:| `change_request_state_conflict` | the revision is not in a state that admits this transition |
1087:| `change_request_evidence_missing` | the named acceptance evidence is not a task-scoped outcome resource, or is not one this reviewer run attached or updated |
1088:| `change_request_checkpoint_conflict` | the Story branch moved under the checkpoint CAS |
1089:| `change_request_checkpoint_index_unsynced` | the managed branch may have advanced, but the real-index owner/lease/CAS or four-identity verification refused; resolve the named condition and retry the same checkpoint |
1090:| `change_request_final_leaf_checkpoint` | the checkpoint would also close the Story; use `worktree integrate`, which lands the branch first |
1091:| `change_request_read_failed` | the record could not be read — this is never treated as "no Change Request" |
1092:| `change_request_acceptance_unauthorized` | the caller is not the reviewer run that read this revision, or its identity could not be established |
1093:| `change_request_sibling_producer_blocked` | another task in this Story holds a Change Request that is not checkpointed: an accepted revision awaiting its checkpoint, a ready or reviewing revision with a non-empty `repository_delta`, or an empty one awaiting republish; review, revise, checkpoint, or `withdraw_cr` that named task before starting this producer |
1094:| `change_request_withdraw_reason_missing` | `withdraw_cr` was called with no written reason; the ledger row is the only surviving explanation of why the revision was never integrated |
